  "limitations": [
    "Proof of concept: 121 Java test cases and 43 mocked Kubernetes Python cases; not the full repository or the 107-minute end-to-end workflow.",
    "Three repetitions for paired Java measurements; dependency downloads and daemon startup excluded. Shared-cache fresh-output and mixed-cache runs measured once.",
    "Bazel and Gradle use Java 21 but different JDK distributions/patch releases. Gradle includes shared test fixture dependencies and different compiler checks.",
    "Default Gradle timings include JaCoCo; a separate three-run execute-no-coverage control measures its effect. Bazel coverage/reporting parity is not implemented.",
    "Shared disk cache recovery demonstrates cross-output-base reuse, not network remote-cache latency or remote execution.",
    "Bazel Java test targets share a module test-classes jar, so edits invalidate at module granularity."
  ],
